Unreleased
~~~~~~~~~~
- share: binkd-compatible shared AKA for netmail failover delivery.
  Config: share <shared-aka> <member1> [member2 ...]
  Fan-out queue/poll to members, ADR/EMSI remote-aka adjustment, and
  rewrite of uncompressed .pkt dest/password to the session peer on send.
- nodelist: if qnode.idx is missing, compile it on query the same way
  as a stale index (ENOENT → NDL_ENEEDCOMPILE). Other open failures,
  a corrupt index, inbound listed-check, and qico -n are unchanged.
- binkplisted: optional nodelist listed-check on BinkP sessions
  (default no). When yes, uses needalllisted like EMSI so `if listed`,
  FREQ listed status and /LST in the options log work on BinkP too.
- emsi: parse/emit the 4-digit EMSI_DAT length and CRC as unsigned, not
  size_t. On LP64, sscanf("%X") into size_t left the high half garbage
  and rejected valid frames with Bad EMSI_DAT length/CRC.
- binkp.h: drop the unused `bp_msg` global from the M_ command enum
  (GCC 10+ -fno-common). -fcommon stays for other legacy commons.
- version: qico -v / EMSI banner date is the UTC git commit time from
  ./configure, not the frozen CVS leftover 2013-02-23 in cvsdate.h.
  Tarballs from make dist keep the stamp in src/source-date; trees
  without git print [unknown].
- zmodem: after a valid HEX-header CRC, accept the frame without
  requiring CR/LF. The trailer is not CRC-covered; many clones omit it
  and the old rhCR/rhLF states turned that into a false BADCRC.
  Leftover CR/LF/XON are skipped as garbage until the next ZPAD. We
  still send the spec CR/LF/XON trailer.
- config: `port' is the outbound-modem switch. When it is set,
  modemconnect must have a usable value or qico refuses to start
  (otherwise Hayes chat never matches CONNECT). Omit every `port'
  line for IP-only. modemok/error/busy and phonetr stay optional.
- config: killconfig() no longer clears the required/nonif bits from
  qconf.x. Startup is rereadconfig(), which used to wipe those bits
  so a missing address/inbound/log/masterlog/nodelist/pidfile passed
  parse and then SIGSEGV'd (cfgal(CFG_ADDRESS)->addr). readconfig()
  now also rejects empty values for those keywords and requires at
  least one of asooutbound/bsooutbound. cfg*() accessors no longer
  dereference a NULL fallback item.


Version 0.59.2-rpe (Rabarber Pie Edition)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Fork baseline freeze before shared-AKA work.
Based on kosfango/qico 0.59.1 plus:
- Debian 12 / modern toolchain: -fcommon, Perl/ncurses via LDADD, 64-bit MD5.
- aarch64 fix: qcc/qctl getopt uses int (unsigned char broke option parsing).
- flagexp/flex: reset lexer between if-expression parses so `if protected`
  selects secure inbound correctly.
- systemd: qico.target + BinkP socket activation (originate + answer).
- osnametemplate: choose which uname() fields (sysname, release, machine)
  go into the auto-detected OS ident; BinkP and other consumers unchanged.


